  What OVER_TCP does (fix):
  tun2proxy still intercepts DNS at the TUN level, but instead of assigning fake IPs it forwards the DNS query as TCP through the proxy. Gets the real domain → real IP mapping back. Now when the app connects to a CDN IP, tun2proxy knows the actual domain name and sends CONNECT rr3.googlevideo.com:443 to PdaNet's proxy. The proxy can reach that. No expiring fake-IP table involved.

